Description: Universal Kernel Manager — CLI
 ukm is a distro-agnostic, architecture-agnostic Linux kernel manager.
 It can install, remove, hold, and manage kernels from the Ubuntu Mainline
 PPA, XanMod, Liquorix, distro-native repositories, Gentoo Portage, and
 local package files.
 .
 Supports apt, pacman, dnf, zypper, apk, and portage package managers,
 covering Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora, openSUSE, Alpine, Gentoo, and
 their derivatives.

Package: ukm-gui
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ukm (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 python3-pyside6 | python3-pyqt6,
Description: Universal Kernel Manager — Qt GUI
 Graphical front-end for ukm. Provides a tabbed window with one tab per
 kernel family (Ubuntu Mainline PPA, XanMod, Liquorix, distro-native,
 Gentoo, local), a unified filtered list, live install/remove log panel,
 and a Gentoo source compilation dialog.
